From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:06:31 -0400
Subject: Translator: Fold constant switch statements

When a switch statement has a constant selector, previously there was no
dead-code elimination done for it in AST.  In IR, cases that would not
be hit were eliminated, but the switch remained with its single matching
case.  Primarily, this was done to avoid having to deal with break and
continue statements nested in the switch.

However, due to driver bugs, a pass is added to completely remove switch
statements that have a constant selector.  Where there are nested break
and continue statements, the switch statement is replaced with a
`while (true) { ... break; }` to allow breaking out of it.  To support
continue statements, a variable is introduced to be set instead of
continue, and the loop is followed by an `if (flag) continue;`.

Some tests are credit zork@

Bug: chromium:548066294
Change-Id: I8b8ad101c37029358c4d4f03282fa463b318c420
